From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:21:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Input: add a driver for the OnePlus pogo-pin keyboard dock

The "Smart Keyboard" dock of the OnePlus Pad 4 (and, by the vendor
device tree, of the OnePlus Pad 3 Pro and the OPPO Pad 5 Pro) talks to
the tablet over a single data line with a private framed protocol at
921600 baud: eight sync bytes, start byte, source and destination
address, command, length, data, a CRC16 (polynomial 0x8005, initial
value 0xc596) and an end sequence. The dock sends a sync frame every
100 ms while it is awake, HID boot keyboard reports, 16 bit codes for
its media keys and touchpad reports with up to five contacts.

Add a serdev driver for it:

- attach detection on the data line read as a GPIO, with the vendor
  driver's timing: line low for 120 ms switches the dock's supply on,
  the first sync frame registers the input devices, 0.5 s without a
  frame switches the supply off again; a line that stays low without
  a dock answering is given up after 20 tries
- the UART is only open while a dock is powered
- frames are sent through the transmit gate; the host hears its own
  frame on the shared line and takes a missing echo as "not sent"
- a keyboard input device (HID usages through the HID core's key
  table, the media key codes, capital lock and mute LEDs, a key map
  that user space can change) and a touchpad input device (multi-touch
  button pad with the size and resolution from the vendor device
  tree, palm reports as MT_TOOL_PALM)
- the keyboard backlight as an LED class device
- system sleep: the dock is told to sleep, a key press or taking the
  dock off wakes the tablet through the data line
- debugfs: status and counters, a trace of the frames (the dock's
  Bluetooth address and serial number masked), a self-test that sends
  one frame through the gate and listens for its echo with an empty
  connector, and a file to send single commands for bring-up

The dock's firmware update is not implemented.

Tested on the OnePlus Pad 4 without a dock (kernel q60, area-combo-52;
first version area-combo-49): the UART runs at 921600 baud, the empty
connector reads high (absent), the dock supply stays off, a 23 byte
frame sent through the transmit gate is heard back on the data line,
the detect edges replayed after the self-test are judged stale,
and the detect line is armed in suspend without ever waking the system.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
